      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion! I tested moving import mdformat to the top of the file, but it unfortunately breaks git cl:\n\n```\n$ git cl\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \".../depot_tools/git_cl.py\", line 52, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    import markdown_format\n  File \".../depot_tools/markdown_format.py\", line 32, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    import mdformat\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \u0027mdformat\u0027\n```\n\nBecause `git_cl.py` globally imports markdown_format early on, putting `import mdformat` at the top causes a crash. The `mdformat` wheels only exist in \n`markdown_format.py`\u0027s local [VPYTHON] block, so the global git cl environment doesn\u0027t have them.\n\nWe could add these wheels to the top-level depot_tools/.vpython3 file, but that would force vpython3 to resolve and verify those heavy dependencies every time any developer runs any `git cl` command. If this is the preferred option, I would be happy to make a change!",
